{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1774228177,"nonce":"c66ZtDn7i5+NHnjo4+eeoym4x9s=","message":"**Framework decision: Fumadocs (Next.js-based)**\n\nChosen for: Tailwind theming, MDX content, file-system routing, decoupled content/styling (can draft content now, style later). Content goes in docs/ as MDX files with meta.json per directory for sidebar ordering.\n\n**Content structure under discussion:**\n\nMultiple documentation axes:\n1. **Getting Started** — installation, first launch, integrating with Claude Code\n2. **Feature Guides** (partitioned by functionality) — Auth Queue, Presets, Console/Chat, History, Issues, Inbox, Switchboard, Graph, Settings\n3. **Architecture** — daemon, UI, Tauri wrapper, tiers (SDK/Channel/PTY/External), Zone 2 split runtime, shared message-blocks library\n4. **API Reference** (low-level, reflects module structure) — auth, presets, sessions/console, runtime, hooks, settings, conversations, issues\n5. **CLI Reference** — mandible, agent-commit, wt/dwt/wt-merge\n6. **Workflow Examples** — multi-agent spec-critique-implement pipelines, bigbuild, labmode experiments\n7. **Other Features** — one-line list for minor cosmetic/preference items\n\nFumadocs handles all of this via nested directories + meta.json ordering. No structural decisions block content drafting.\n\nPlatform paths for comparison: ~80KB/page (lighter than Nextra/Docusaurus), sub-second builds, full Tailwind customization.","files":null}]}